                <pb facs="0260" n="154" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg154"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Egan to Mr.
                            Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-08-27"><hi rendition="#italic">August 27,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Egan telegraphs that the revolutionists were victorious in a fierce battle
                    near Valparaiso last Friday and that a decisive engagement was expected on the
                    day of the sending of his telegram. He states that there is no communication
                    between Valparaiso and Santiago and says it is <pb facs="0261" n="155"
                        xml:id="pg155"/> very important that he be informed by telegraph of any
                    early reliable news which the Department might receive. Thinks it may be
                    possible to stop further bloodshed.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
